Ms by human preference\",\n419\t    \"Judging LLM-as-a-judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena human pairwise judgments\",\n420\t    \"Understanding black-box predictions via influence functions\",\n421\t    \"Cook's distance case deletion diagnostics one-step approximation logistic regression\",\n422\t    \"adversarial vote manipulation of LLM arena leaderboard rankings\",\n423\t    \"robustness of rankings from pairwise comparisons to adversarial or corrupted comparisons\"\n424\t  ],\n425\t  \"reference_query_plan\": {\n426\t    \"architectural_shifts\": [],\n427\t    \"benchmarks\": [\n428\t      \"Chatbot Arena human preference battles (55k / 140k)\",\n429\t      \"MT-Bench human expert judgments\"\n430\t    ],\n431\t    \"central_topic\": \"Citation gaps in a paper on minimal removal sets (verified by exact Bradley-Terry refit) that flip adjacent-pair rankings of pairwise-comparison leaderboards: the Chatbot Arena / MT-Bench data and platforms, influence-function and case-deletion diagnostics behind the first-order removal ranking, and manipulation or corruption of crowd-vote and pairwise-comparison rankings.\",\n432\t    \"comparators\": [\n433\t      \"influence-only row removal (B2 comparator)\",\n434\t      \"adversarial manipulation and vote rigging of crowd-vote leaderboards\",\n435\t      \"robustness of pairwise-comparison rankings to corrupted comparisons\"\n436\t    ],\n437\t    \"core_methods\": [\n438\t      \"first-order (one-step Newton) influence of deleting a row on the Bradley-Terry score gap, with leave-one-out leverage correction\",\n439\t      \"case-deletion diagnostics (Cook's distance style) for logistic-type likelihoods\"\n440\t    ],\n441\t    \"forbidden_query_patterns\": [\n442\t      \"generic optimization or benchmarking surveys\",\n443\t      \"scientific method or paper-writing phrasing\",\n444\t      \"chronology of cycles, attempts or search history\",\n445\t      \"internal score names such as combined_score or rubric\",\n446\t  